.TH SUBBER 1.SH NAMEsubber \- substitute words from a list.SH SYNOPSIS\fBsubber\fRwordlist [file].SH DESCRIPTION\fBsubber\fRcopies a file, or the standard input, to the standard output replacingwords by the pairs in\fIwordlist\fR.\fREach line of the word list is one pair written\fB,old,new\fR:\fRits first character is the delimiter, so\fB/a,b/c\fRworks as well when a pair contains a comma..SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR\fBsubber\fRgrows its data area with F$Mem as it reads the word list, and needs roomabove it to do that.  Give it memory when you start it, with Microware'sshell's own directive:.nf    subber #1000k words letter.fiThe\fB#1000k\fRis read by that shell, not by\fBsubber\fR,\fRso under another shell it runs out of memory at once..SH SEE ALSOsed, tr